{"4220620": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "The Last Frame", "steam_appid": 4220620, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Light is your only point of orientation.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In <i>The Last Frame</i>, darkness is ever-present. Candles and torches are the only tools to make spaces visible. Every light source expands your view — and simultaneously alters what is perceived.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are no hints and no certainties. Light can reveal a path or distort it. Every decision determines what remains visible.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4220620/extras/d6eea8cd343526b7c4a16c42583359f3.poster.avif?t=1769375150\" width=800 height=450 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4220620/extras/d6eea8cd343526b7c4a16c42583359f3.webm?t=1769375150\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4220620/extras/d6eea8cd343526b7c4a16c42583359f3.mp4?t=1769375150\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>The more you hold on, the less remains hidden.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >With each photograph, you move closer to the trace of your missing father. The images do not preserve memories — they reconstruct what was left behind.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The photographs provide direction, but they also demand attention. The longer you hold on, the harder it becomes to suppress the feeling that something is looking back.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>In the end, only the last frame matters – and what remains of it.</strong> </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A dense, roughly one-hour journey without detours: From the church to the d